Detecting physical and emotional states through JavaScript is a complex task, and there is no specific library or API that can do this accurately. However, there are some ways to detect certain physical states, such as heart rate or body temperature, by using sensors or wearable devices that can be connected to your computer or mobile device.
Regarding emotional states, there are some natural language processing libraries that can analyze text and detect emotions based on the words and expressions used. One example is the Sentiment Analysis API provided by RapidAPI.
To incorporate environmental factors such as temperature and humidity, you can use APIs that provide real-time weather data, such as OpenWeatherMap or Weather Underground.
Here is a sample code snippet that uses the Sentiment Analysis API and OpenWeatherMap API to detect your emotional state and the current weather conditions, and modify the sentence "I'm feeling relaxed" accordingly:
```javascript
const sentence = "I'm feeling relaxed";
const apiKeySentiment = 'your_sentiment_analysis_api_key';
const apiKeyWeather = 'your_openweathermap_api_key';
// Get sentiment analysis
fetch(`https://api.rapidapi.com/sentiment/api/v1/analyze?text=${sentence}`, {
 method: 'GET',
 headers: {
 'x-rapidapi-host': 'sentiment-analysis.p.rapidapi.com',
 'x-rapidapi-key': apiKeySentiment
 }
})
.then(response => response.json())
.then(data => {
 const sentiment = data.sentiment;
 let newSentence = sentence;
 // Modify sentence based on sentiment
 if (sentiment === 'positive') {
 newSentence = "I'm feeling great";
 } else if (sentiment === 'negative') {
 newSentence = "I'm feeling down";
 }
 // Get weather data
 fetch(`https://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5/weather?q=your_city_name&appid=${apiKeyWeather}`, {
 method: 'GET'
 })
 .then(response => response.json())
 .then(data => {
 const temperature = data.main.temp;
 const humidity = data.main.humidity;
 // Modify sentence based on weather conditions
 if (temperature > 25 && humidity > 60) {
 newSentence += " and it's hot and humid outside";
 } else if (temperature < 10) {
 newSentence += " and it's cold outside";
 }
 console.log(newSentence);
 });
});
```
Note that you need to replace `your_sentiment_analysis_api_key`, `your_openweathermap_api_key`, and `your_city_name` with your own API keys and city name. Also, this is just a sample code snippet, and you may need to modify it to fit your specific use case.

