Here's the C# code to calculate the potential environmental and economic benefits of investing in public transportation based on the given data:
```
using System;
class Program
{
 static void Main(string[] args)
 {
 // Given data
 double carCO2Emissions = 4.6; // metric tons per year
 double avgTransportationCost = 9576; // in USD per year
 double busPassCost = 75; // in USD per month
 int busCapacity = 50; // passengers per bus
 // Calculate the potential annual reduction in CO2 emissions
 int passengersPerYear = 12 * busCapacity; // passengers per year per bus
 double CO2ReductionPerPerson = carCO2Emissions; // metric tons per year
 double CO2ReductionPerYear = passengersPerYear * CO2ReductionPerPerson;
 Console.WriteLine("The potential annual reduction in CO2 emissions if all passengers switch from cars to the bus is " + CO2ReductionPerYear + " metric tons.");
 // Calculate the potential collective savings in transportation costs per year
 double busPassCostPerYear = 12 * busPassCost; // in USD per year
 double savingsPerPerson = avgTransportationCost - busPassCostPerYear; // in USD per year
 double savingsPerYear = passengersPerYear * savingsPerPerson;
 Console.WriteLine("The potential collective savings in transportation costs per year is $" + savingsPerYear + ".");
 // Calculate the potential economic benefit of investing in public transportation
 int jobsCreatedPerBus = 5; // assuming 5 jobs per bus
 int totalJobsCreated = jobsCreatedPerBus * passengersPerYear;
 double economicActivityIncrease = savingsPerYear; // assuming all savings are spent on other goods and services
 Console.WriteLine("The potential economic benefit of investing in public transportation in terms of job creation is " + totalJobsCreated + " jobs.");
 Console.WriteLine("The potential economic benefit of investing in public transportation in terms of increased economic activity is $" + economicActivityIncrease + ".");
 }
}
```
Here are the calculations:
- Potential annual reduction in CO2 emissions: 
 - Passengers per year = 12 (months) * 50 (passengers per bus) = 600
 - CO2 reduction per person = 4.6 (metric tons per year)
 - CO2 reduction per year = 600 * 4.6 = 2760 metric tons
- Potential collective savings in transportation costs per year:
 - Bus pass cost per year = 12 * $75 = $900
 - Savings per person = $9576 - $900 = $8676
 - Savings per year = 600 * $8676 = $5,265,600
- Potential economic benefit of investing in public transportation:
 - Jobs created per bus = 5 (assumption)
 - Total jobs created = 600 * 5 = 3000
 - Economic activity increase = $5,265,600 (savings per year)

